{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalActionExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalActionExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction.exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction.exists","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action-exists.lean#L47-L67","doc":"**The categorical action of the identity is the bare pairing loop.**\n\nFor the identity endomorphism the whiskered factor drops out, so\n`𝒮_{𝟙} = η_ ≫ swap ≫ ε_` — the categorical trace of `𝟙`, i.e. the\ncategorical dimension of `A` relative to `swap`.\n\n**Why this statement and not \"the action exists\".** The previous form\nwas `∃ S : 𝟙 ⟶ 𝟙, S = categoricalAction Φ swap`, discharged by\n`⟨categoricalAction Φ swap, rfl⟩`. Its own docstring conceded that\n*\"'exists' and 'equals tr(Φ)' hold by construction\"* — which is the\npoint: `∃ S, S = e` is provable by `⟨e, rfl⟩` for any `e`, so it made\nno claim about `categoricalAction`. Existence of a named composite is\nnot a theorem; the definition above already supplies it. This\nreplacement is falsifiable — it would fail if whiskering by `𝟙` did\nnot act as the identity. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-action-exists","label":"prop:categorical-action-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.categoricalAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.categoricalAction","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action-exists.lean#L36-L45","doc":"**Categorical action** `𝒮_Φ : 𝟙 ⟶ 𝟙` of a Lagrangian endomorphism `Φ : A ⟶ A`.\n\n`𝒮_Φ = η_ ≫ (Φ ▷ Aᘁ) ≫ swap ≫ ε_`, the composite\n`ev_A ∘ (id_{Aᘁ} ⊗ Φ) ∘ coev_A` of the manuscript, with `swap` the\ntransposition `A ⊗ Aᘁ ⟶ Aᘁ ⊗ A` supplied alongside the pairing.\nThis is, by definition, the categorical trace `tr(Φ)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}